# gitleaks baseline — historical-finding suppression for the ENFORCING gate
#
# Authority: SPRINT CC-7 (chain-of-custody-closure Phase 2), operator ruling R-3.
#   BUILD-cc7-gitleaks-biting-gate-2026-08-14.md
#   CRITIQUE-cc6-gitleaks-recon-2026-08-13.md §5.2 (CF-5 baseline scope)
#   RECON-gitleaks-enforcement-locus-2026-08-13.md §2 corollary
#
# WHAT THIS IS. Every line below is a gitleaks FINDING FINGERPRINT of the form
#   {commit-sha}:{file-path}:{rule-id}:{start-line}
# Fingerprints are keyed on the (commit, file, rule, line) tuple — NOT on a bare
# commit SHA, NOT on a path glob, and NOT on a secret value. No credential value
# appears in this file, and none may ever be added to it (CR-5).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. `gitleaks detect` walks the FULL git history (checkout
# fetch-depth: 0, no --log-opts range restriction). Every historical finding in
# this repo's history trips on every run, forever — history is immutable, so
# rotating a credential does NOT green the scan (gitleaks pattern-matches
# history, it does not validate token liveness). Without this baseline the
# enforcing job at .github/workflows/gitleaks-enforcing.yml is red on day one
# and blocks every merge to main.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. This baseline suppresses ONLY the exact historical
# (commit, file, rule, line) tuples enumerated below. A NEW secret introduced in
# ANY new commit produces a NEW fingerprint that is NOT in this list, and the
# enforcing gate goes red. That two-sidedness is the whole point: the baseline
# unblocks CI on inherited history without blinding the gate to new leaks. It is
# also orthogonal to credential ROTATION, which is a separate, operator-reserved
# remediation and is neither performed nor discharged by this file.
#
# MAINTENANCE. Do not add entries by hand and do not add path/rule globs. To
# extend, re-run the enforcing scan, export the JSON report to a scratch path
# OUTSIDE the repo, and lift ONLY the `.Fingerprint` field via jq. The report
# body carries secret values; it must never be committed, printed, or pasted.
#
# Baseline snapshot: 49 fingerprints across 26 commits and 22 files,
# generated from origin/main d75601531edd220e693ce279f10b2a9b1d171f20
